ontract that (a) the API binary does not terminate TLS itself and\n   501\t(b) t
he rate limiter trusts only a closed set of forwarded-IP\n   502\theaders. Three
real-file matchers run alongside one synthetic\n   503\tself-check (`TestHTTPSer
verHardeningStaticAnalyzerDetectsRegressions`):\n   504\t\n   505\t- **`cmd/yall
a-api/main.go`** — `findAPITLSRegressions` walks the\n   506\t  AST and rejects:
(1) any call whose selector name is in\n   507\t  `forbiddenAPITLSCallSelectors`
(`ListenAndServeTLS`, `ServeTLS`),\n   508\t  regardless of receiver; (2) any `h
ttp.Server` composite literal\n   509\t  that omits a field from `requiredHTTPSe
rverFields`\n   510\t  (`ReadHeaderTimeout` is the Slowloris guard) OR contains 
a field\n   511\t  from `forbiddenAPITLSStructFields` (`TLSConfig`, `TLSNextProt
o`);\n   512\t  (3) any assignment whose LHS selector is in\n   513\t  `forbidde
nAPITLSStructFields` (the post-construction mutation\n   514\t  seam). The match
er uses the package-qualified type selector\n   515\t  `http.Server`, so unrelat
ed structs in `main.go` are not scanned.\n   516\t- **`internal/controlplane/htt
papi/ratelimit.go`** —\n   517\t  `findProxyHeaderTrustRegressions` runs two pas
ses. The scoped\n   518\t  pass locates the `ClientIP` function by name and walk
s every\n   519\t  `*.Header.Get("...")` inside it; any literal not in\n   520\t
 `allowedProxyHeaderLiterals` (`X-Forwarded-For`, `X-Real-IP`,\n   521\t  case-s
ensitive) is flagged. The scoped pass also asserts the\n   522\t  body reference
s `RemoteAddr` so the fallback chain stays intact.\n   523\t  The file-wide pass
walks every string literal in the file and\n   524\t  flags any whose lower-case
d form is in\n   525\t  `forbiddenProxyHeaderLiterals` (RFC 7239 `Forwarded`,\n 
 526\t  `True-Client-IP`, `CF-Connecting-IP`, `Fastly-Client-IP`,\n   527\t  `X-
Client-IP`, `X-Forwarded-{Host,Proto,Server,Port}`,\n   528\t  `X-Original-Forwa
rded-For`). If `ClientIP` is missing entirely\n   529\t  the matcher emits a sin
gle "missing function" hit so the gate\n   530\t  cannot pass silently when its 
target is removed.\n   531\t- **`SECURITY.md`** —\n   532\t  `TestHTTPServerHard
eningSecurityDocumentsTLSAndProxyTrust` pins\n   533\t  the `## TLS Termination 
and Proxy Header Trust` heading, the\n   534\t  verification-gates table row, an
d the canonical substrings\n   535\t  (`TLS is terminated at the operator\'s rev
erse proxy`,\n   536\t  `ReadHeaderTimeout`, `X-Forwarded-For`, `X-Real-IP`, and
the\n   537\t  test file path itself). The substrings carry the load-bearing\n  
538\t  facts so a future reader does not have to open the test file to\n   539\t
 learn the contract.\n   540\t\n   541\tWhen adding or removing a trusted forwar
ding header, update\n   542\t`allowedProxyHeaderLiterals` AND the `ClientIP` bod
y AND the\n   543\tSECURITY.md section in the same edit. When adding or removing
