\n    21\t   redacted log excerpts.\n    22\t3. The impact you observed (token l
eak, RCE, denial-of-service,\n    23\t   privilege escalation, etc.).\n    24\t\
n    25\tYou will receive an acknowledgement within **3 business days**. We aim\
n    26\tto ship a fix or mitigation within **30 days** for high-severity\n    2
7\tissues; lower-severity issues are folded into the next scheduled\n    28\trel
ease.\n    29\t\n    30\t## Supported Versions\n    31\t\n    32\tPre-1.0 yalla 
supports only the latest minor release line on\n    33\t[GitHub Releases](https:
//github.com/JuribaDev/yalla/releases). Once\n    34\tyalla reaches 1.0 the matr
ix will be published here.\n    35\t\n    36\t## Threat Model and Hard Rules\n  
 37\t\n    38\tYalla is invoked by AI agents in unattended pipelines. The follow
ing\n    39\tproperties are part of the public contract and are enforced by the\
n    40\ttest suite:\n    41\t\n    42\t- **Secrets never reach stdout.** `--jso
n` data on stdout, all\n    43\t  diagnostics on stderr. The `--token` value, we
ll-known transport\n    44\t  patterns (`Authorization`, `X-Api-Key`, `X-Auth-To
ken`), and\n    45\t  `?token=`/`?api_key=` query strings are scrubbed by\n    4
6\t  `internal/output.Redactor` before any byte is written.\n    47\t- **Errors 
are typed.** Every user-visible failure is an\n    48\t  `internal/errors.Error`
with a stable `Code` and exit code. Plain\n    49\t  `fmt.Errorf` reaching stder
r is a contract violation.\n    50\t- **`--no-input` never hangs.** When the fla
g is set, any prompt path\n    51\t  exits with `E_NO_INPUT_REQUIRED` (exit code
9) instead of blocking.\n    52\t- **Releases are reproducible.** Archives are b
uilt by GoReleaser in\n    53\t  GitHub Actions; checksums are published alongsi
de every release.\n    54\t  The npm wrapper, Homebrew formula, Scoop manifest, 
and WinGet\n    55\t  manifest all resolve to the same archives.\n    56\t\n    
