aser-check` job | Every push and PR |\n   135\t\n   136\tBefore cutting a tag th
e maintainer additionally runs:\n   137\t\n   138\t- `scripts/verify.sh --releas
e` locally — runs every check above plus\n   139\t  `goreleaser release --snapsh
ot --clean`.\n   140\t- A manual review of the dependency diff since the last ta
g\n   141\t  (`go list -m -json all` baseline).\n   142\t- A spot-check of `yall
a manifest --json` to confirm no schema\n   143\t  removals or exit-code remappi
ngs have slipped in unintentionally.\n   144\t\n   145\tIf a verification tool i
s missing locally, `scripts/verify.sh` reports\n   146\tit explicitly. The repos
itory\'s policy is **never silently skip a\n   147\tcheck** — an absent tool mus
t either be installed or noted in\n   148\t`ralph/progress.txt` so the gap is vi
sible.\n   149\t\n   150\t## Dependency Review Expectations\n   151\t\n   152\tY
alla pulls only what it needs. When you add or update a third-party\n   153\tGo 
module, follow the checklist in\n   154\t[`CONTRIBUTING.md`](./CONTRIBUTING.md#d
ependency-review-checklist) and\n   155\texpect the dependency-review CI job to 
gate the PR. New modules with\n   156\tunknown licenses or known high-severity a
dvisories will be rejected\n   157\tautomatically.\n   158\t\n   159\t## Contain
er Image Hardening\n   160\t\n   161\tThe production `Dockerfile` ships the `yal
la-api` binary and\n   162\t`Dockerfile.worker` ships the `yalla-worker` binary 
inside a\n   163\t`gcr.io/distroless/static-debian12:nonroot` runtime so a leake
d or\n   164\tcompromised image carries no shell, no package manager, no busybox
,\n   165\tand no setuid binaries — only the service binary and the system CA\n 
 166\tbundle. The hardening posture is part of the public contract and is\n   16
7\tpinned by `internal/release/container_hardening_static_test.go`; a\n   168\tr
egression in any one of the following is caught at build time:\n   169\t\n   170
\t- **Multi-stage build.** The Go toolchain, module cache, and source\n   171\t 
tree never reach the runtime layer. A single-stage Dockerfile is\n   172\t  reje
cted.\n   173\t- **Distroless `nonroot` runtime.** The runtime stage\'s base ima
ge\n   174\t  is pinned to `gcr.io/distroless/static-debian12:nonroot` (UID/GID\
n   175\t  65532). Debian/Ubuntu/Alpine slim runtimes are rejected because\n   1
76\t  they reintroduce a shell and a package manager.\n   177\t- **`USER nonroot
:nonroot`.** The runtime stage MUST run as the\n   178\t  non-root user. A missi
ng or partial (`USER nonroot`) directive is\n   179\t  rejected.\n   180\t- **Ha
rdened build flags.** The builder stage MUST invoke\n   181\t  `go build` with `
CGO_ENABLED=0` (static binary compatible with\n   182\t  the distroless static i
mage), `-trimpath` (strip local filesystem\n   183\t  paths from the binary), an
d `-ldflags="-s -w"` (drop the symbol\n   184\t  and DWARF tables). Each missing
flag is a separate regression.\n   185\t- **No `ADD <url>`.** Fetching arbitrary
content at build time\n   186\t  without checksum verification is forbidden. Use
`COPY` or a\n   187\t  `RUN curl ... | sha256sum -c` pattern.\n   188\t- **No ba
ked secrets.** The Dockerfile MUST NOT declare ENV values\n   189\t  whose key n
ames contain `TOKEN`, `PASSWORD`, `SECRET`, `API_KEY`,\n   190\t  `PRIVATE_KEY`,
`SIGNING_KEY`, or `DSN`. Secrets are supplied by\n   191\t  the operator at runt
ime through environment variables, never\n   192\t  baked into the image.\n   19
3\t- **No package install in the runtime stage.** `apt-get`,\n   194\t  `apt ins
tall`, `yum install`, `dnf install`, `microdnf install`,\n   195\t  and `apk add
` are rejected in the final layer. The builder stage\n   196\t  is free to insta
ll build dependencies; the runtime stage is not.\n   197\t- **`COPY --from=build
er --chown=nonroot:nonroot`.** Every\n   198\t  cross-stage COPY into the runtim
e layer MUST chown to the\n   199\t  non-root user so the copied artefact is not
owned by root.\n   200\t- **Explicit `ENTRYPOINT`.** The runtime stage MUST decl
are an\n   201\t  `ENTRYPOINT` (not just `CMD`) so `docker run -- <args>` cannot
\n   202\t  replace the binary at launch.\n   203\t- **Worker image contract.** 
`Dockerfile.worker` MUST build\n   204\t  `./cmd/yalla-worker`, copy `/out/yalla
-worker` to\n   205\t  `/usr/local/bin/yalla-worker`, and use that binary as the
\n   206\t  entrypoint. The worker has no HTTP listener, so orchestrators\n   20
7\t  should use process liveness, non-zero exit restarts, durable\n   208\t  pro
visioning job state, dead-letter alerts, worker queue metrics,\n   209\t  and st
ructured `service=yalla-worker` logs instead of an in-image\n   210\t  HTTP heal
th probe.\n   211\t\n   212\tOperators are expected to run the image with `--rea
d-only`,\n   213\t`--cap-drop=ALL`, and a non-host network. The Dockerfile\'s he
ader\n   214\tcomment documents the canonical `docker run` invocation; the worke
r\n   215\tDockerfile documents the corresponding no-port runtime contract.\n   
216\t\n   217\tThe local operations stack (`docker-compose.yml`) MUST keep the\n
  218\tPostgres-only integration-test workflow available while also\n   219\tver
sioning an opt-in `control-plane` profile for `yalla-api` and\n   220\t`yalla-wo
rker`. The Postgres image is pinned to a major version tag\n   221\t(`postgres:1
6`, not `postgres` and not `postgres:latest`) and\n   222\tdeclares a `healthche
ck` so the integration-test harness has a\n   223\tdeterministic readiness gate.
The API and worker services build from\n   224\tthe production `Dockerfile` / `D
ockerfile.worker`, wait for\n   225\t`postgres.condition=service_healthy`, run w
ith a read-only root\n   226\tfilesystem, `cap_drop: [ALL]`, `no-new-privileges:
true`, and a `/tmp`\n   227\ttmpfs, and use required environment-variable interp
olation for every\n   228\tsecret-shaped value. `yalla-api` publishes `8080:8080
` so operators\n   229\tcan probe `GET /healthz` and `GET /readyz`; `yalla-worke
r` still has\n   230\tno HTTP listener and is observed through structured stdout
logs plus\n   231\tdurable job state.\n   232\t\n   233\t## Kubernetes Operation
s Artifact\n   234\t\n   235\tThe production Kubernetes baseline lives at\n   23
6\t`deploy/kubernetes/yalla-control-plane.yaml` with the operator runbook in\n  
237\t`deploy/kubernetes/README.md`. The artifact references the hardened\n   238
\t`ghcr.io/juribadev/yalla-api` and `ghcr.io/juribadev/yalla-worker`\n   239\tim
ages, runs both pods as non-root with a read-only root filesystem,\n   240\tdrop
s all Linux capabilities, disables service-account token mounting,\n   241\tand 
uses `RuntimeDefault` seccomp.\n   242\t\n   243\tThe checked-in manifest intent
ionally does **not** include a Kubernetes\n   244\t`Secret`. Runtime credentials
are bound by `secretKeyRef` from the\n   245\toperator-created `yalla-control-pl
ane-secrets` object so database URLs,\n   246\tsigning keys, Dokploy endpoints, 
and Dokploy tokens are never baked into\n   247\timages or repository files.\n  
248\t\n   249\t`yalla-api` exposes `/healthz` and `/readyz` on port 8080 for Kub
ernetes\n   250\tliveness and readiness probes. `yalla-worker` has no HTTP liste
ner; its\n   251\thealth model is process liveness, durable job state, worker me
trics, and\n   252\tstructured JSON logs. Operators can render the artifact offl
ine with\n   253\t`kubectl kustomize deploy/kubernetes` or validate it against a
cluster with\n   254\t`kubectl apply --dry-run=server -f deploy/kubernetes/yalla
-control-plane.yaml`.\n   255\tCI pins the contract with\n   256\t`go test ./int
ernal/release/... -run TestKubernetesArtifact`.\n   257\t\n   258\t## systemd Op
erations Artifact\n   259\t\n   260\tThe single-node systemd baseline lives unde
r `deploy/systemd/` with separate\n   261\tunits for `deploy/systemd/yalla-api.s
ervice` and\n   262\t`deploy/systemd/yalla-worker.service`. The API unit execute
s\n   263\t`/usr/local/bin/yalla-api`; the worker unit executes\n   264\t`/usr/l
ocal/bin/yalla-worker`. Both run as the dedicated non-root `yalla`\n   265\tserv
ice account, load runtime configuration from\n   266\t`/etc/yalla/control-plane.
env`, and write structured JSON diagnostics to\n   267\tjournald.\n   268\t\n   
269\tThe checked-in units intentionally do **not** include database URLs, signin
g\n   270\tkeys, secret-encryption keys, Dokploy endpoints, or Dokploy tokens. O
perators\n   271\tcopy `deploy/systemd/control-plane.env.example` to\n   272\t`/
etc/yalla/control-plane.env`, replace the `<redacted:...>` placeholders from\n  
273\ttheir secret manager, and keep the rendered file outside the repository wit
h\n   274\tmode `0640` and group `yalla`.\n   275\t\n   276\tBoth units preserve
a least-privilege sandbox: `NoNewPrivileges=true`,\n   277\t`ProtectSystem=stric
t`, `ProtectHome=true`, private temporary and device\n   278\tnamespaces, empty 
capability sets, native syscall architecture, and address\n   279\tfamilies limi
ted to `AF_UNIX`, `AF_INET`, and `AF_INET6`. `yalla-api` binds\n   280\t`127.0.0
.1:8080` by default for a local TLS-terminating reverse proxy and\n   281\texpos
es `GET /healthz` plus `GET /readyz`; `yalla-worker` has no HTTP listener\n   28
2\tand is observed through process liveness, durable job state, worker metrics,\
n   283\tdead-letter alerts, and structured logs.\n   284\t\n   285\tOperators c
an dry-run the unit syntax with\n   286\t`systemd-analyze verify deploy/systemd/
yalla-api.service deploy/systemd/yalla-worker.service`.\n   287\tCI pins the art
ifact with\n   288\t`go test ./internal/release/... -run TestSystemdArtifact`.\n
  289\t\n   290\t## Database Migration Command Artifact\n   291\t\n   292\tThe p
roduction database migration command lives at\n   293\t`deploy/operations/migrat
e-database.sh` with the runbook in\n   294\t`deploy/operations/README.md`. It ru
ns the API binary\'s embedded migration\n   295\trunner through `/usr/local/bin/
yalla-api --migrate-only`, so the SQL ladder\n   296\tapplied in production is e
xactly the version compiled into the backend\n   297\trelease. The worker binary
remains separate: the script stops `yalla-worker`\n   298\tbefore applying schem
a changes and restarts both `yalla-api` and\n   299\t`yalla-worker` after a succ
essful migration.\n   300\t\n   301\tThe command loads runtime configuration fro
m `/etc/yalla/control-plane.env`\n   302\tor `YALLA_CONTROL_PLANE_ENV_FILE`. It 
never checks in or prints database URLs,\n   303\tsigning keys, secret-encryptio
n keys, Dokploy endpoints, Dokploy tokens, API\n   304\tkeys, cookies, or render
ed environment values; `--dry-run` prints only command\n   305\tshape plus redac
