okArtifact`.\n   883\t\n   884\t## TLS Termination and Proxy Header Trust\n   88
5\t\n   886\tThe Yalla control-plane API binary (`cmd/yalla-api`) deliberately\n
  887\tdoes NOT terminate TLS itself.\n   888\t**TLS is terminated at the operat
or\'s reverse proxy**\n   889\t(ingress controller, load balancer, or front-door
proxy), which\n   890\tforwards the request to the API over an internal network.
Keeping certificate material out of the API process\n   891\tnarrows the secret 
surface, leverages the proxy\'s vetted cipher\n   892\tsuite / HSTS / OCSP stapl
ing defaults, and lets operators rotate\n   893\tcertificates without an API res
tart. The posture is pinned by\n   894\t`internal/release/http_server_hardening_
static_test.go`; a regression\n   895\tin any one of the following is caught at 
build time:\n   896\t\n   897\t- **No in-process TLS.** The API binary MUST NOT 
call\n   898\t  `ListenAndServeTLS` or `ServeTLS`, and the constructed\n   899\t
 `*http.Server` MUST NOT set `TLSConfig` or `TLSNextProto`. Any\n   900\t  TLS-t
ermination shape inside the binary is rejected.\n   901\t- **Slowloris guard.** 
Every `*http.Server` literal in the API\n   902\t  binary MUST set a positive `R
eadHeaderTimeout`. The current value\n   903\t  is `10 * time.Second`. Removing 
the field, or initialising the\n   904\t  server with the zero value, is rejecte
d.\n   905\t- **Closed-set proxy header trust.** The rate limiter resolves the\n
  906\t  caller\'s identity through `ClientIP(r)` in\n   907\t  `internal/contro
lplane/httpapi/ratelimit.go`. The helper consults\n   908\t  only two forwarding
headers:\n   909\t  - `X-Forwarded-For` — the **first hop only** is taken so a f
orged\n   910\t    tail entry cannot displace the real client.\n   911\t  - `X-R
eal-IP` as a fallback.\n   912\t  No other forwarded-* family header is honoured
. RFC 7239\n   913\t  `Forwarded`, Akamai `True-Client-IP`, Cloudflare\n   914\t
 `CF-Connecting-IP`, Fastly `Fastly-Client-IP`, `X-Client-IP`,\n   915\t  `X-Ori
ginal-Forwarded-For`, and the meta-data variants\n   916\t  (`X-Forwarded-Host`,
`X-Forwarded-Proto`, `X-Forwarded-Port`,\n   917\t  `X-Forwarded-Server`) are de
liberately ignored. If the API is\n   918\t  ever reachable directly — a network
misconfiguration, an internal\n   919\t  pivot, or a forgotten test fixture — an
attacker who can reach it\n   920\t  must not be able to spoof their identity pa
st the IP bucket by\n   921\t  sending one of those headers. The closed set is e
nforced by the\n   922\t  static analyser; adding a new header to the trust list
requires\n   923\t  an explicit, reviewed change to the allow-list.\n   924\t\n 
 925\t### Operator expectations\n   926\t\n   927\tThe reverse proxy MUST be con
figured to:\n   928\t\n   929\t1. **Strip inbound `X-Forwarded-*` and `X-Real-IP
` headers** from\n   930\t   public traffic before setting its own. Otherwise an
attacker\n   931\t   can pre-populate the header and the proxy will forward it\n
  932\t   verbatim — the API will then trust the attacker-supplied value.\n   93
3\t2. **Set `X-Forwarded-For`** to the immediate downstream client\'s\n   934\t 
 IP address. The API only reads the first hop, so the proxy\'s\n   935\t   appen
d-on-each-hop semantics are honoured.\n   936\t3. **Terminate TLS** with a moder
n cipher suite, an up-to-date\n   937\t   certificate, and HSTS where appropriat
e. The API never sees\n   938\t   the original ClientHello.\n   939\t4. **Use an
internal network or loopback** to reach the API. The\n   940\t   API listener is
HTTP-only and MUST NOT be exposed to the\n   941\t   public internet directly.\n
  942\t\n   943\t## Admin Endpoint Isolation\n   944\t\n   945\tThe Yalla contro
l-plane API binary (`cmd/yalla-api`) deliberately\n   946\tships **no `/debug/` 
surface**. There is no `/debug/pprof/*`, no\n   947\t`/debug/vars`, no `/debug/r
equests`, and no `/debug/events` route on\n   948\tthe customer-facing listener 
— neither authenticated nor\n   949\tunauthenticated. Goroutine profiles, heap s
napshots, command-line\n   950\targuments, registered `expvar` variables, and li
ve CPU profiles are\n   951\tload-bearing operator-only secrets; exposing any of
them on a\n   952\tlistener customers can reach is a build-blocking regression. 
The\n   953\tposture is pinned by\n   954\t`internal/release/admin_endpoint_isol
ation_static_test.go`; the\n   955\tgate rejects any of the following shapes at 
build time:\n   956\t\n   957\t- **No side-effecting debug imports.** Neither `c
md/yalla-api` nor\n   958\t  any production source file under `internal/controlp
lane/httpapi`\n   959\t  may import `net/http/pprof`, `expvar`, or\n   960\t  `g
olang.org/x/net/trace`. A blank import alone is sufficient to\n   961\t  registe
r the surface on `http.DefaultServeMux`; the matcher\n   962\t  rejects every fo
rm of import (blank, named, aliased) of those\n   963\t  three paths.\n   964\t-
**Private mux only.** `httpapi.NewHandler` MUST construct its own\n   965\t  mux
via `http.NewServeMux()` and MUST NOT reference\n   966\t  `http.DefaultServeMux
` anywhere. The private mux severs the API\n   967\t  listener from any default-
mux registrations made elsewhere in the\n   968\t  binary (a transitive dependen
cy, a hand-rolled experiment, a\n   969\t  future contributor\'s debugging helpe
r). The matcher flags the\n   970\t  absence of `http.NewServeMux()` and any ref
erence to\n   971\t  `DefaultServeMux` in the handler file.\n   972\t- **Explici
t `http.Server.Handler`.** The API binary\'s\n   973\t  `*http.Server` composite
literal in `cmd/yalla-api/main.go` MUST\n   974\t  set `Handler` to a non-nil va
lue. A nil `Handler` falls back to\n   975\t  `http.DefaultServeMux` per the sta
ndard library\'s documented\n   976\t  contract, and that fallback would re-intr
oduce the exposure the\n   977\t  private-mux contract disclaims. The matcher fl
ags both the\n   978\t  missing field and an explicit `Handler: nil`.\n   979\t-
**No `/debug/*` literal or `pprof.*` / `expvar.*` selector.** No\n   980\t  prod
uction source file under `cmd/yalla-api` or\n   981\t  `internal/controlplane/ht
tpapi` may carry a `/debug/pprof`,\n   982\t  `/debug/vars`, `/debug/requests`, 
or `/debug/events` string\n   983\t  literal, name `http.DefaultServeMux`, or re
ference a `pprof.*` or\n   984\t  `expvar.*` selector. The file-wide pass is bel
t-and-braces for\n   985\t  the import scan: a regression that registers the rou
tes through\n   986\t  a hand-rolled handler or a vendored fork would still leav
e the\n   987\t  path literal in source.\n   988\t\n   989\tThe runtime evidence
half is implicit: any `/debug/*` request that\n   990\tslips past the gates is i
ntercepted by `notFoundRecorder` in\n   991\t`internal/controlplane/httpapi/serv
er.go` and returned as the\n   992\tstable `yalla.error.v1` envelope with code `
E_NOT_FOUND`, while\n   993\t`telemetry.RequestLogging` records the rejected req
uest in the\n   994\tredacted structured log. The static analyser ensures we nev
er\n   995\tregister the surface in the first place; `notFoundRecorder` is the\n
  996\tdefence-in-depth wall.\n   997\t\n   998\tThe set of legitimate operator-
visible routes on the API listener\n   999\tis closed and documented in the Open
API document served at\n  1000\t`GET /openapi.json`: `GET /healthz`, `GET /ready
z`,\n',
